<!--Post: 1752--><!--Time: 1102796894-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1752"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bodycheck<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bodycheck<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, December 11, 2004 - 12:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->hate to follow up on my own post...but, i thought id elaborate on my reasoning... <BR> <BR>If the guy knew which kid to stop and ask for directions... one would think the killer had seen the victim AND her together, I would hope the cops or other investigators would see this and researched her life in the previous weeks/months.. somewhere the killer interacted with her or observed her and her family and decided to make her a victim, if not that...there is some connection that made him seek her out and research her enough to identify her and her family... this just seems like such a glaring fact that i am amazed nothing ever came of it... do the cops have info related to this victim that has the key and just overlooked it?...or did they just flat out miss it... <BR> <BR>thoughts? <BR> <BR>B<!--/Text--></td></tr>
