<!--Post: 2020--><!--Time: 1103252102-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2020"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jim44095<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jim44095<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 6:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->where and when would he have gotten a photo of her?  <BR> <BR>Maybe he worked at a photomat and knew them from there,can&#39;t think of the name of the Robin Wiliams movie where he worked at a drugstore and kept the photos of the that family.This guy seems to have way to much info about photography,he could also get the chemicals and bring them home or develope them at work and nobody else would see them.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
